        "principle": "A Black Swan is always relative to a specific observer, not an objective property of an event, and Taleb links the failure to grasp this to a mild, systematizing form of mind blindness akin to Asperger syndrome; he then argues that, because true uncertainty can never be fully separated from mere incomplete knowledge, probability has to be treated as a subjective degree of belief rather than an objectively measurable quantity.",
