        "principle": "Ethical independence requires having no one vulnerable whose fate depends on your choices; Taleb argues that family, institutional ties, and other people's exposure to your decisions are what let the powerful pressure the principled into silence, which is why truly free actors (celibates, the financially independent, the reputation-proof) are so rare.",
