        "title": "How to Be Rational About Rationality",
        "principle": "Rationality cannot be judged from stated beliefs; it can only be judged from actions and, ultimately, from what allows a person or system to survive, which is why beliefs that look 'irrational' on paper (superstitions, rituals, dietary taboos) often turn out to be sound risk-management heuristics in disguise.",
